          "message": "fix(velvet)!: stack equal z in tree order, negate a bracket z and clamp one beyond the int range (#1400)\n\n## What & why\n\n- Equal `z-*` values stack in tree order, as CSS does: the sibling declared later paints on top, also after a keyed reorder or when an earlier sibling mounts later. They used to stack in the order they first mounted. A post-pass re-sort of each layer replaces the mount-order tiebreak.\n- A leading `-` negates a bracket value (`-z-[5]` is -5), as Tailwind v4 emits it.\n- A value beyond the 32-bit integer range stacks at that end of it, as CSS clamps it (`z-2147483648`), instead of leaving the class unresolved. Main's rule that the one Tailwind emits last wins among important or plain `z-*` classes is kept.\n- A `z-*` change that keeps an element in the same layer re-sorts it with `Hierarchy.Sort`, so it raises no `DetachFromPanelEvent`.\n- The layer teardown and re-sort run at the end of every top-level pass, including each slice of a time-sliced pass, in a `finally` of their own: a throw from either still reaches the pointer-events release, the queue clears and the abort reset.\n\nRefs #1119 (Z17, partly): a change within one layer no longer detaches the element. Gaining or losing a z, and flipping the sign, still detach it. Each of those moves the real element to a different parent (the stacking parent, the front container or the back container), and UI Toolkit's `WillChangePanel` runs on every parent change; only a reorder within one parent avoids it. Closing the rest would need an element to live in a layer container whatever its z, which changes every absolute element's hierarchy and is not a change of this size.\n\nDocumentation: `styling-z-index.md` updated (clamp, tree order, resort timing). CHANGELOG: breaking fragment `fix-1119-z-scale-ported.md`, since stacking order of equal-z siblings changes for a working application.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run locally; CI runs both suites\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — left to `Test ▸ base-red` and the mutation campaign\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-`\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — Z17's remaining transitions stay on #1119\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
