          "distinct": true,
          "id": "24dd9832b43561c2e8353fff17707a8d2bfa2517",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: remove an AnimatePresence child on a render after the one that removed it (#1399)\n\n## What & why\n\nFramer Motion's `AnimatePresence` drops a child only on a render after its exit completes. Velvet removed a child with nothing to animate (no `V.Motion`, `StyleTransitionConfig.None`, a zero-duration exit, or a spring exit with no channel to drive) in the very render that removed it. Now:\n\n- Such a child stays for the removing commit, and its exit completes from the passive-effect flush after it; the render that settle asks for drops the child. A removal whose commit never ran completes nothing and is staged again by the next render that still removes the child.\n- A walk that aborts stages its settle again rather than restarting the exit, and a dropped ghost's fibers are disposed only once its walk commits.\n- Under `AnimatePresenceMode.Wait`, while a removed child exits the presence renders the exiting children alone, as `mode=\"wait\"` does.\n- The exits one commit leaves with nothing to animate settle in Framer's order, which decides how `onExitComplete`'s error is routed (a boundary, or the log when the last exit settled belongs to a `V.Motion`). A motion child's exit naming no target, or one reached with a zero-duration or `type: false` transition and no delay, resolves from its promise (motion-dom `animateMotionValue` skips the animation, so `animateTarget` collects none). A child holding no motion component settles from `PresenceChild`'s passive effect. For a removal from a discrete event (the Urgent lane) the effect settles first, because react-dom flushes the passive effects of a commit whose lanes include `SyncLane` at the end of that commit (`commitRootImpl`); for any other lane the promise settles first. The previous revision of this branch put an instant-target exit on a later frame, which Framer does not do; that phase is gone.\n- A child mounted leaving gets a stagger slot only when its exit plays.\n\n`FiberWorkLoop.IsRenderingUrgentLane` carries the lane of the flush that renders; the pending completion records it when it is queued.\n\nSpot-checked against motion-dom `main` and react-dom 18.3.1; the motion-dom 12.x tag was not read.\n\nDocumentation: `Documentation~/motion.md` (the removal and `onExitComplete` bullets) is updated; `StyleTransitionConfig.None` and `HasExitAnimation` docs say \"after the commit\". Branch `fix/1114-spring-duration-ported` edits the same `HasExitAnimation` text and the `motion.md` line on an exit whose delta resolves no channel; both here read \"after the commit\".\n\nCHANGELOG: breaking fragments `Changelog~/breaking/fix-presence-removes-on-a-later-render.md` (and the amended `claude-issue-1112-aborted-walk.md`), since a working application sees a child leave one render later.\n\nTests: new cases pin the removal timing, the abort and Wait paths, and the settle order per lane kind (`BoundaryCatchScopeTests`: non-discrete and discrete, for an instant pose and for a no-target Motion). Assertions that packed two facts into a tuple are split into one fact per case. No Unity editor was available while writing this; the suites have not been run locally and CI must show them.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run locally, no editor; CI runs them\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — left to `Test ▸ base-red` and `Test ▸ unity-tests`\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none found\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
