          "message": "fix(velvet)!: decline a bare non-zero length in a bracket, and type a bracket as Tailwind does (#1418)\n\n## What & why\n\nPart 2 of a stack that splits a branch too large to review in one pull request. Part 1 is on `main` as #1404,\nand this part is built on `main`.\n\nThe browser rejects a unitless length other than `0`, and Tailwind writes a bracket such as `w-[120]` through as\n`width: 120`, so the class does nothing there. Velvet read the bare number as pixels for every length bracket;\nit now reads only a bare `0`.\n\nWhere Tailwind reads a bracket as either a length or a colour, a port of its data-type tests\n(`infer-data-type.ts`) decides: `border-*` takes a number and the line-width keywords `thin`, `medium` and\n`thick`; `text-*` a percentage and the font-size keywords; `outline-*` a number or a percentage, which the\nbrowser drops as a width while keeping the solid style, so the outline draws at medium; `ring-*`,\n`ring-offset-*` and `from-` / `via-` / `to-` a length alone. Anything else is a colour to Tailwind and inert.\nThe digit scan of that port is bounded by the string's length.\n\nThe cases that asked whether a unit is spelled as Tailwind infers it ask `TailwindDataTypes.IsLength`, which\nreplaced that predicate, and the duplication and logic-refusal baselines are regenerated for the change.\n\nThe behaviour change that leaves a class inert is in the breaking changelog fragment.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run here: no Unity editor was available; `Test ▸ unity-tests` and `Test ▸ base-red` are what measure them\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — left to `Test ▸ base-red`\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (`styling-arbitrary-lengths.md`)\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` (`unreleased/` and `breaking/`)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none found\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
