          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c712f8987f991c129b8dacb4e0d0b1b35b37a0f7",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: let a V.Motion own the slots it animates (#1435)\n\n## What changed\n\nWhile a `V.Motion` animates a length or a colour, the animated value now takes precedence over:\n- the element's variant layers (`dark:`, `sm:`, `hover:` …);\n- a `space-*` margin;\n- a `divide-*` colour or width;\n- the width a grid column gives a child.\n\nThis matches CSS, where an animation outranks those rules. When the play releases the slot, the element's own value returns.\n\nAn important declaration of the element's own (`!w-[80px]`, `hover:!w-[80px]`) and an important divide colour keep what they win, because `!important` outranks an animation. The play's own important pose does not outrank the play, since its end value is what the play moves toward. That includes the pose an interrupted exit reverses to.\n\nGaps and margins:\n- A gap now adds to an animated margin, as CSS adds an item's margin to its gap. This covers a grid's column and row gaps, and an element's important margin that wins over the animation.\n- A grid takes a driven margin out of the child's column width, so the child moves inside its column instead of wrapping the row.\n\nBefore this change:\n- A variant toggling mid-play replaced the animated value until the next frame, or for the rest of a delay.\n- A gap or grid replaced an animated margin.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe cases run through the real drivers:\n- `MotionPropertyChannelTests`: variant and important layers against a width drive.\n- `GapParityTests`: release, gap arrival, wrapping rows, grid column gaps, and an important margin arriving.\n- `DivideClassParityTests`: divider colour against a drive and against an important divide colour.\n- `CompositeWidgetSpacingDirectionPanelTests`: a percentage margin, and a grid child moving inside its column on a real panel.\n- `ChildVariantBoxOwnershipTests`: a delayed grid spring.\n- `PresenceReversalLabelChangeTests`: an interrupted exit away from an important pose reverses rather than snapping.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- `motion.md` and `styling-flexbox-and-gap.md` are updated.\n- CHANGELOG: breaking fragment.\n\nRefs #1118\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
