          "distinct": true,
          "id": "34bd44d4da3d0c67f12f0c393c436d67ee277060",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: subscribe store hooks in the commit's passive effects (#1437)\n\n## What changed\n\n`Hooks.UseSyncExternalStore` and `Hooks.UseStore` now subscribe in the commit's passive effects, as React's `useSyncExternalStore` does, instead of during render.\n\nWhat a render reads reaches the effects and notifications only once that render settles. So these subscribe nothing and cannot change what an earlier commit's pending effects use:\n- a render whose body throws or suspends;\n- an attempt that a render-phase update re-runs;\n- a render that a Suspense gives up.\n\nOther timing changes:\n- A store change between the render and the subscription is caught when the subscription compares the snapshot.\n- A `UseSyncExternalStore` re-render that a sync-lane commit's passive effects ask for renders in the same drain and counts toward the update-depth cap, as in React.\n- Under StrictMode, the mount's `subscribe` is double-invoked.\n\nThe test helpers now run pending passive effects first, as React's `act()` does: `FlushStateForTest` always, and `DrainImmediateForTest` when its tier is empty. `V.Mount` is unchanged.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- `react-migration.md`: the useEffect row and the external stores section.\n- `AGENTS.md`: the note on the test helpers.\n- Breaking fragment: `Changelog~/breaking/fix-subscribe-at-commit.md`.\n\nStacked on #1436.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
