          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2edf1fa9988f04eb83a2568be1fcf8c438f667bf",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: discard what the browser rejects in a declaration Tailwind composes (#1433)\n\nPart 4 of the stack whose earlier parts are #1404, #1418 and #1429.\n\n## What changed\n\nWhen Tailwind composes several utilities into one shared declaration, a single value the browser rejects invalidates that whole declaration. Velvet now discards such values the way the browser does. It discards only what the browser rejects. A value Velvet merely cannot read, such as `var()`, `oklch()`, `currentColor`, a colour name Unity does not list, or a length unit Velvet cannot place, keeps its previous behaviour.\n\n- **Box-shadow (breaking).**\n  - These values invalidate the shared box-shadow:\n    - a ring or ring-offset colour that is not a colour;\n    - a ring width that is not a length, including `ring-[length:0]` and `ring-[length:50%]` inside the ring's `calc()`;\n    - an `inset-ring-*` value the browser rejects;\n    - a `shadow-[…]` or `inset-shadow-[…]` layer that breaks the box-shadow grammar;\n    - a rejected shadow colour that a preset reads.\n  - When that happens, the ring and every `shadow-*` on the element are discarded. A `drop-shadow-*` is a filter, so it stays.\n  - A colour-typed `shadow-[…]` writes only the shadow colour, as Tailwind emits it.\n- **Gradient stops (breaking).** A `from-`, `via-` or `to-` colour the browser rejects leaves its stop transparent. A rejected position returns the stop to its registered initial value.\n- **Composed families (breaking).**\n  - These families are composed through one declaration: `translate-*`, `scale-x/y-*` with `scale-<n>`, `skew-*`, and the filters.\n  - A family is judged per element, on the value each custom property holds after importance, variants and Tailwind's rule order:\n    - An important rejected value drops the family.\n    - A rejected value that another value overrides drops nothing.\n    - A rejected value under a variant turns the family off while that variant applies. This also covers co-active variant sets, through stacked prefixes. It is done with variant-scoped tokens that set each property to a value that does nothing.\n  - A plain `rotate-[…]` or `scale-[…]` that the browser rejects takes nothing else with it.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `RejectedValueTests` covers ring, shadow and inset discards and gradient stops. It has characterization controls for values Velvet cannot read.\n- `RejectedCompositeTests` covers families that are dropped, overridden, under a variant, and under co-active variants, plus families that are kept.\n- `FilterSurvivorReapplyTests` pins that two blurs follow Tailwind's emit order.\n- `ArbitraryValueTests` pins that a bare `w-[200]` is declined.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- `styling-arbitrary-lengths.md` gains the section \"A rejected value\".\n- Breaking fragment: `Changelog~/breaking/fix-caret-selection-alpha-modifier-4.md`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
