          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3a8b84719329ed5428dfd8735b0e548be46e7dd3",
          "message": "fix(velvet): draw a layoutId Motion's class-changed scale, rotate and origin from the first frame (#1443)\n\nRefs #1116\n\n## What changed\n\n**L-b.** When a render changes a layoutId Motion's classes and gives it the lead, its first frame is now drawn with the new own scale, rotate and origin. This applies when they come from Velvet's bundled utility classes, and only where no other stylesheet rule could set them. Before, that first frame still used the old values, because UI Toolkit's style pass runs after the render's projection.\n- Gated (`hover-*`/`active-*`) classes, `anim-*` classes and the application's own rules still take effect from the style pass, as before.\n- A lead moving from another holder's box mixes its rotate towards the new class value from that frame.\n- A class change re-projects only when the scale, rotate or origin read off the classes changes.\n\n**L-a.** Still approximate, now with the reason stated in `motion.md`. Drawing it exactly needs a 3D tilt, and a tilted element would not take the pointer on parts of its drawn face, because picking maps the pointer at depth zero and a Motion has no per-element picking override.\n\n**L2, L3, L-c.** Already matched Framer Motion on main.\n\n## Docs\n\n`motion.md`, `player-builds.md` (engine members read by name), and a fragment in `Changelog~/unreleased`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
