          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3c83b18a6dacc6de1a698ea0e304f49eabaedf56",
          "message": "fix(velvet): render the preview window through a runtime panel so its pixels match a player's (#1445)\n\nCloses #1128\n\n## What changed\n\nThe preview window now renders each story on a runtime panel. That panel is built from the chosen PanelSettings and drawn into a texture, which the canvas shows. As a result, the panel, viewport, font, backdrop and theme conditions are the ones a player has, and the preview's pixels match it. Canvas pointer, wheel, key and navigation events are sent on to that panel, and the Outline and Measure overlays are mapped through it. The smoke test uses the same panel type.\n\n`VelvetPreviewPanel` is new public API.\n\n## Docs\n\n`preview-tooling.md` gains a Rendering section and drops the deviation that said the preview's pixels need not match. A fragment is added in `Changelog~/unreleased`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
