          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d398e679402c2c2a9fe1a3c3fff06d9c7d2be31d",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: run passive effects in tree order, throw at the update-depth bound, and route boundary and Suspense faults as React does (#1450)\n\n## What changed\n- A commit's passive effects run in its layout order (tree order), also after a keyed reorder moves components (H22, H26).\n- Nested updates are bounded at 50 commits and throw \"Maximum update depth exceeded\"; the scheduler cap throws instead of logging and dropping (H23).\n- A component whose first render threw is disposed (H19).\n- A fault below an error boundary inside a Suspense re-renders the Suspense (H24).\n- A suspend inside a fallback goes to the Suspense above the one showing it (H27).\n- H15, H16, H21 and H25 were already resolved on main; the doc rows now say so.\n\nBreaking changes are recorded in `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1112-parity.md`.\n\n## Docs\n`react-migration.md` (`useEffect`, `getDerivedStateFromError`, Suspense).\n\nCloses #1112\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
