          "distinct": true,
          "id": "31b26e76c9bb9dcd3ba2cf59d04f6354929ac454",
          "message": "fix(velvet): add the backdrop-* filters, read any whole number and em/vw in filter utilities, and keep a transform-origin transition across filter writes (#1448)\n\nCloses #1120\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`backdrop-*` filter family.** `backdrop-blur-*`, `-brightness-*`, `-contrast-*`, `-grayscale-*`, `-hue-rotate-*`, `-invert-*`, `-opacity-*`, `-saturate-*`, `-sepia-*`, `backdrop-filter-none` and `backdrop-filter-[…]` now filter what lies behind an element, inside its rounded border box, with the element's own background, border and children painted over the result. Each class was inert before. An immediate-mode layer (`Velvet/BackdropFilter`, `BackdropRenderer`, `StyleBackdropClass`, `FiberBackdropApplier`) is placed directly before the element, carries its transform, opacity, visibility and display, and sits inside every ancestor clip and the element's own `clip-path-*`. The family writes one declaration, held by the class Tailwind emits last; the functions compose in Tailwind's order, `url()` runs as no function, and a negative blur makes the declaration invalid. Changes transition under an `all` entry by CSS's filter-list interpolation. It renders on a `RenderTexture` panel, a screen-space overlay panel and an editor window's panel; a world-space panel draws none, because UI Toolkit refuses an immediate-mode element there (`WorldSpaceImmediateModeTests` pins the refusal).\n- **Any whole number in the filter families.** `brightness-*`, `contrast-*`, `saturate-*`, `grayscale-*`, `invert-*`, `sepia-*` and `hue-rotate-*` take any whole number, as Tailwind v4 does, not only the old preset values.\n- **`em`, viewport units and math functions in `blur-[…]` and `drop-shadow-[…]`.** They are measured on the element and measured again when its font size or the panel size moves.\n- **A running transform-origin transition survives filter and background-size writes.** A filter change that lands at once, and a gradient, clip path or projected corner face sizing the background, no longer end a running transform-origin transition. No `filter` or `background-size` transition runs for such a write; the earlier single `TransitionRunEvent` for `filter` on an element with no filter is gone (Group G of `FilterTransitionPanelTests`).\n- **Fixes the backdrop layer needed.** Unmounting an element carrying a backdrop layer no longer throws (`FiberElementCleaner` and the portal teardown remove each cleaned element by reference), and a `z-*` element's border overlay keeps its place directly after the element when the layer resorts.\n- **No limit on a backdrop blur or shadow deviation.** A deviation whose reach exceeds the shader's 1024 texels is blurred on a copy halved until it fits and drawn back up, for `blur()` and `drop-shadow()`; `BackdropFilterPlaybackTests` samples a pixel 1100px beyond the edge under a 1000px deviation.\n- **Filter-parameter cap.** A `FilterFunction` holds at most 4 parameters; `CustomFilterRegistryTests` pins that the engine throws on a fifth, so the registration check stays and the doc names that test.\n\n## Where the other #1120 items stand\n\nAlready closed before this branch: FL3, FL9 (`Register`, re-registration and `Unregister` re-resolve mounted elements), FL13 (list interpolation by position, discrete otherwise), FL15 (clear and set are timed by the entry the engine reads for each), the FL1 `pt` remainder, the FL5 remainder, the second FL16 (detach mid-fade), FL17 (filter clears go through `StyleFilterEngineWrite`) and FL18 groups, and `drop-shadow-*`.\n\n## Docs\n\n`styling-filters.md` (backdrop section, bracket grammar, transform-origin note), `styling-arbitrary-lengths.md`, `player-builds.md`. Changelog fragment: `Changelog~/unreleased/fix-1120-filter-parity.md`. No breaking fragment: no existing class changes meaning.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
