          "distinct": true,
          "id": "945dfc1df528c983cbd6968c38a7b3972af257c9",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: Framer Motion parity for layoutId shared layout (#1456)\n\nCloses #1116\n\n## What changed\n- A `layoutId`'s last box is kept after its last holder leaves, so a Motion that mounts under the id in a later batch tweens from it instead of appearing in place. Retained boxes are bounded and indexed by parent, so pooling a parent touches only its own ids.\n- A rotated `layoutId` Motion inside another that stretches by different factors on its two axes is drawn undistorted: its counter-scale and move sit in a wrapper outside its own rotate. The wrapper is created with the Motion, or swapped in and out in place when the gate changes, and a running tween hands on the box it is drawn at.\n\nBreaking changes: `Changelog~/breaking/claude-issue-1116-layoutid-snapshot.md`, `Changelog~/breaking/claude-issue-1116-layoutid-rotated-correction.md`. `Documentation~/motion.md` updated.\n\n---\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
