          "committer": {
            "email": "noreply@github.com",
            "name": "GitHub",
            "username": "web-flow"
          },
          "distinct": true,
          "id": "26778e94352f5d4333bc83c0fba1c4425e3d7f76",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: text and typography parity with CSS (#1460)\n\nCloses #1121\n\n## What changed\n- A text leaf keeps the app's text. The engine is handed the effect string as rendered text, so `label.text` is no longer rewritten. When rich text is off, a leaf shows its text without the decoration and line-height tags instead of the literal markup.\n- An ancestor's text decoration reaches its descendants, and `no-underline` on a descendant no longer removes it.\n- Added `leading-[normal]`.\n- `text-[150%]` and `tracking-[50%]` are measured against the font size.\n- Added `font-stretch-*`, matched against a font weight entry's stretch.\n- `tracking-*` presets are em of the element's own font size; `leading-[…]` reads viewport units and em/percent math; `antialiased` / `subpixel-antialiased`; `tabular-nums` / `proportional-nums` / `normal-nums` through `<mspace>`; font-family lists onto fallback tables; overline on the line top; `enableRichText` changes and start/middle ellipsis show the effect string. The OpenType variants that need GSUB selection are documented with the TextCore source that shows no way to select them.\n\nBreaking changes are in `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1121.md`; `Documentation~/fonts.md` is updated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
