          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5d282ef72b266af5708779edb2ca4705793ee1eb",
          "message": "fix(velvet): paint ring-inset under children and follow container markers written by hand (#1463)\n\n## What & why\n\n**`ring-inset` paints under the element's children, as an inset box-shadow does.**\n- Before, the band was a following sibling, so it painted over an opaque full-bleed child.\n- It is now the element's own first child, stretched over the padding box and rounded to the padding box's corners, the element's radii less the adjoining border. Its radii are re-synced on each state tick, so a border-width change with no geometry event still refits them.\n- Child counts, structural variants (`[&>*]:`, `*:`), gap/grid/divide logic and later-rendered children all leave it first.\n- Being a child, it no longer copies the element's opacity or transform, which would apply them twice.\n- The outset ring is unchanged.\n\n**z-layer resort keeps leading internal children first.**\n- `FiberZLayerCoordinator.BuildDesiredOrder` placed any unplaced child after the front band, so a z-* resort moved a leading internal child to the end.\n- It now keeps the inset band, a SceneView feed and Particles layers first.\n\n**A container variant follows a container marker written straight to a class list.**\n- This covers `AddToClassList(\"@container\")` / `RemoveFromClassList`, named containers included.\n- Before, such a marker took effect only at the marked element's next render, which never comes for an element that renders nothing of its own.\n- Now an element carrying a container variant polls its nearest container while attached, and re-points within a frame when that changes.\n- Only those elements poll, and a tick builds no enumerator or string.\n\nDocs: `Documentation~/styling-variants.md` (the ring-inset and container-marker lines). Changelog: `Changelog~/unreleased/fix-ring-inset-under-children.md`, `Changelog~/unreleased/fix-container-marker-by-hand.md`.\n\nCloses #1117\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable). Not run locally (no Unity editor available); CI `Test ▸ unity-tests` is the verification.\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it. Measured by `Test ▸ base-red` on this PR.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
