          "distinct": true,
          "id": "afbca29a9d5261ceb1ceca7b21d6043dae132527",
          "message": "feat(velvet)!: Tween plays follow sequence controls on the realtime clock and play their Repeat (#1473)\n\n## What & why\n\nA `Tween` play ignored `Repeat`: it played once and logged a warning. On the realtime clock it also ignored a sequence's Pause, Speed and Cancel.\n\n- **Driver routing:** a `Tween` play on a `MotionPlayback`, or one with `Repeat` above zero, now runs on the Velvet-driven tween driver (`StyleAnimationScheduler.RunsDriven`). The sequence controls therefore reach it on `MotionClock.Realtime`, as they already reach Spring and Bezier plays.\n- **Repeat:** `BezierTweenDriver` plays Loop, Reverse and Mirror passes over the Tween's easing, waiting out the delay once. The \"plays once\" warning is removed.\n- **Sequence holds:** a sequence step and a `BeforeChildren` parent wait out a repeating Tween (`SequenceWalker`, `MotionPlaySpan`).\n- **Docs:** `Documentation~/motion.md` and the `README.md` row; the earlier repeat fragment's now-false sentence is corrected. Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/feat-1268-tween-controls.md`.\n\nCloses #1268\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — the Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via the base-red lane\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
