          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d595f40153b78c8baa4058e948395cb93f18b1a2",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: compose a stylesheet's rotate or scale into a skewed element (#1469)\n\n## What & why\n\nOn a skewed element, a rotate or scale that a user stylesheet declared was dropped: the composite read only the inline slots and the bundled class list.\n\n- `BundledClassTransform.OfRules` now reads the unset slots from the rules the last style pass matched (`StyleCascade.Rotation` / `StyleCascade.Scale`), still beneath the inline slots. It falls back to the class list when the bundled sheet is not attached.\n- `AuthoredTransform` composes again on `CustomStyleResolvedEvent` whenever the matched rotate or scale changes. A skewed element carries `velvet-skew-observed` so that the event fires for it.\n- A rotate about an axis other than z is declined and documented.\n- Docs: the limitation in `Documentation~/styling-variants.md` is replaced by this behaviour.\n- Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1467-stylesheet-skew-compose.md`, since such elements now draw differently.\n\nCloses #1467\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — the Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via the base-red lane\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
