          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a0f41d87679e3cbcf023488ccbdd04c31083aaf8",
          "message": "feat(velvet)!: await mutation callbacks, share query results structurally, add cache commands (#1475)\n\n## What & why\n\nThree query behaviours diverged from TanStack Query v5:\n\n- **Mutation callbacks:** `OnMutate`, `OnSuccess`, `OnError` and `OnSettled` were synchronous.\n  - They now return a `VelvetTask` and each stage is awaited. `OnMutate`'s result becomes the context.\n  - A faulted callback task fails the call, and the outcome commits after the last callback.\n  - Per-call `MutateOptions` callbacks stay synchronous, as in v5.\n- **`PlaceholderData`:** it now takes `(previousData, QueryInfo? previousQuery)`.\n- **Structural sharing:** it now reaches application classes and records, field by field. An equal instance keeps its identity, and a changed one becomes a shallow clone that carries the equal members.\n  - It also applies to `Select` and placeholder output.\n  - `StructuralSharing` becomes `Func<object?, object, object>`.\n\nAdditive:\n- `QueryClient` gains `RefetchQueries`, `CancelQueries`, `RemoveQueries`, `ResetQueries`, `FetchQuery`, `PrefetchQuery`, `EnsureQueryData`, `GetQueryState`, `GetQueriesData` and `SetQueriesData`, with `QueryFilters`.\n- `InvalidateQueries` returns a task that completes when its refetches settle.\n\nDocs: `Documentation~/react-migration.md` and the index. Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/feat-1325-query-parity.md` and `Changelog~/unreleased/feat-1325-query-parity.md`.\n\nThe remaining additive items of #1325 stay open there.\n\nRefs #1325\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — generator tests locally; Unity suites in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via the base-red lane\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
