          "id": "e5dc9686a09515b4dc38f47c629fb7be0c783a69",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the mutation survivors in the particle driver and effect view (#1481)\n\n## What & why\n\nThe mutation record holds 34 survivors in `ParticlesDriver.cs` and `ParticlesEffectView.cs`. They are answered as follows.\n\n- **`ParticlesBlendLayerTests`** (new):\n  - draw-order ties, and a renderer-off system that adds no run;\n  - layer teardown and shrink on repatch, and a destroyed child dropping its blend;\n  - target and live extents;\n  - the tick repainting blend layers, and Stop ending logical play;\n  - the position and left styles of a created layer.\n- **`ParticlesEffectViewTests`** (new):\n  - hide flags on the clone and the camera, an inactive child's renderer, the premultiplied layer material, and the lowest free layer;\n  - the no-layer advisory logged once;\n  - Manual recorded as applied, and Stop clearing the initial event;\n  - the initial event restored on a Manual-to-Mount flip;\n  - references released on repatch to null;\n  - the camera aspect at a pixel scale other than 1.\n- **Declarations in `ParticlesDriver.cs`** (six equivalent, one unreachable). Each states why no caller can observe the difference, or why the state cannot be reached.\n\nStill unanswered:\n- `ParticlesEffectView.cs:115`, the `Reinit` call in `Stop`. Nothing observable without a VFX graph.\n- `ParticlesDriver.cs:827`. Its mutant loops forever and times out, so no test can answer it.\n\nTest-only apart from the declaration comments; no doc or changelog impact.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — kills are decided by the next mutation record run\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
