          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6856020cc370b5ec48dee78620fb8fa4bd88cbb1",
          "message": "perf(velvet): make clearing a keyed list linear in its rows (#1491)\n\n## What & why\n\nClearing or replacing N rows of a list cost O(N^2), from two per-removed-row costs:\n\n- `FiberElementCleaner.CleanupElement` -> `ComponentRegistry.DisposeFibersUnder(VisualElement)` tested every registered fiber's `MountPoint` ancestor chain against the removed element. The registry now selects the fibers by walking the removed subtree and reading `_tenancies` / `_wrapperIndex` (indexes keyed by the container a fiber mounts on, equal to its `MountPoint`). The multi-root overload (Suspense rollback, one call per rollback) keeps the scan.\n- The removal loops in `ChildReconciler` and `GeneralPathReconciler.FinalizeGeneralCommit` resolved each row's physical index with `LogicalChildSlots.ToPhysical`, a walk from the first child that runs `IsInvisible` (nine class-list checks) per child. They now hold a `DescendingSlotCursor`, which walks on from the slot resolved before and falls back to the full walk when the child preceding the remembered slot has moved.\n\nTests (`KeyedListClearScalingTests`, `DescendingSlotCursorTests`): clearing 100 vs 200 inline rows must grow the container's child reads, and its hashes (one per fiber checked by the old scan), by less than 2.5x. Counts, not timing. The cursor cases pin its answers against the static walk. I could not run Unity locally; the reds are for CI base-red to show.\n\nNot changed: `FiberElementCleaner.RemoveCleaned` still does `parent.IndexOf` (O(N) compares per removal); `ComponentFiber.AppendChild`/`RemoveChild` walk the sibling chain.\n\nBenchmark medians (js-framework-benchmark keyed ops, from #1489 merged with this branch) are in a comment below once the run finishes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run locally, no editor available; CI runs them\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via CI base-red\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches — no doc impact (internal reconciler cost; the one comment in `LogicalChildSlots` that named the quadratic loops is updated)\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — the two listed above are not yet filed\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
