          "distinct": true,
          "id": "caf20a50efa9003ae672db73b5d25e211f1df3dd",
          "message": "test(velvet): pin the retry of a suspended pass through memoized layers (#1496)\n\n## What & why\n\nBuilds on #1493 (base is `main`, so the diff shows that PR's commits until it merges).\n\nTwo follow-ups on the retry of a pass that suspended with no boundary, which now asks the reading fiber to render after the retried ancestors. Both were traced from the code and neither needed a production change; this PR adds the two cases that pin them.\n\n- A chain `outer -> inner (memo) -> mid (memo) -> reader`: the retry bails on `inner`, and the reader, dirty from the retry's request, keeps `inner`'s patch alive (the dirty check walks every descendant fiber), so it renders the resolved value. The case is `Given_AnUpdateThatSuspendedTheReaderBelowTwoMemoizedComponentsWithNoBoundary_...`.\n- Render count: the immediate tier drains in tree-depth order, ancestors first, so the retried ancestor's pass renders the reader and settles its request; the reader's own entry is then skipped. The case is `Given_AReaderBelowTwoMemoizedComponentsWhoseAncestorsPassSuspended_...`, expecting one render.\n\nBoth are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`. Neither was run: no editor was available, so CI is their first run.\n\nDocs: no impact (tests only; the fixture summary gained one sentence). CHANGELOG: no fragment, nothing user-visible changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (generator suite 545 + 16 passed; EditMode not run, no editor)\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it (not applicable: characterization cases, no production change)\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches, or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment: none, tests only\n- [x] No deferrals discovered that need an issue\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
